│ patch_name               │ tied_butterfly_mixer                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz replaces the deep nearest-neighbor CZ chain with a three-stage multiscale     │
│                          │ butterfly of trainable CRY interactions. The stages connect adjacent, distance-two, and   │
│                          │ distance-four qubits, allowing information to propagate across all eight qubits with      │
│                          │ logarithmic interaction depth. Control directions are balanced so each qubit participates │
│                          │ as both a control and a target.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Independent RY rotations preserve local adaptability, while two parity-shared RZ          │
│                          │ parameters provide phase sensitivity with strong regularization. Sharing one interaction  │
│                          │ parameter across each butterfly scale reduces the unique parameters per block from 24 to  │
│                          │ 13. The resulting circuit is shallower, uses fewer gates, and should reduce overfitting   │
│                          │ and convergence cost while retaining global expressivity.                                 │
