│ patch_description        │ This ansatz uses a trainable correlation-injection layer rather than relying solely on    │
│                          │ fixed CZ gates for entanglement. Four disjoint CRY gates share one parameter, adding      │
│                          │ pairwise input-dependent interactions with only one extra trainable angle per repeated    │
│                          │ block. The open CZ chain then propagates these correlations globally, while parity-shared │
│                          │ pre-rotations regularize the model and independent post-rotations preserve readout        │
│                          │ flexibility. This targets improved validation accuracy without a large parameter or depth │
│                          │ increase.                                                                                 │
