│ patch_name               │ collapse_redundant_phase_sandwiches                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Collapse the two RZ–CZ–RZ sandwiches into one CZ ring followed by independently           │
│                          │ parameterized per-wire RZ gates. Because CZ commutes with RZ, the current parity-shared   │
│                          │ pre/post rotations reduce to only two effective phase combinations while introducing      │
│                          │ redundant optimization directions and many extra gates. The replacement preserves full    │
│                          │ ring entanglement, restores eight identifiable local phase degrees of freedom at the same │
│                          │ total parameter count, and substantially reduces gate count, which should improve         │
│                          │ expressivity, conditioning, and convergence.                                              │
