│ patch_description        │ Add a parity-shared RX mixer after the final phase sandwich. The current tail consists    │
│                          │ entirely of commuting RZ/CZ operations, so a noncommuting mixer should convert learned    │
│                          │ phase correlations into measurable population differences and improve expressivity        │
│                          │ without substantially increasing parameter count. Sharing one angle across even wires and │
│                          │ one across odd wires adds only two parameters per repeated block, preserving              │
│                          │ regularization and fast convergence.                                                      │
