│ patch_description        │ Restore parity sharing in the pre-entanglement RZ layer, which previously improved the    │
│                          │ combined score while reducing parameter count and convergence time. Then add a            │
│                          │ lightweight parity-shared RY mixing layer immediately after the CZ chain. Unlike the      │
│                          │ surrounding diagonal RZ/CZ operations, these RY gates change computational-basis          │
│                          │ populations, increasing useful nonlinearity with only two additional parameters per       │
│                          │ repeated block. Parity sharing regularizes the circuit and keeps the added expressivity   │
│                          │ parameter-efficient.                                                                      │
