│ patch_description        │ Collapse the two consecutive parity-shared RZ layers into one, since adjacent rotations   │
│                          │ about the same axis are algebraically redundant. Reinvest the two saved parameter         │
│                          │ identities by giving the second RY mixing layer independent parity parameters. This       │
│                          │ preserves the parameter count while reducing gate count and depth, removing an            │
│                          │ ill-conditioned redundant parametrization, and allowing the two entangling stages to      │
│                          │ learn distinct nonlinear transformations.                                                 │
