                         Patch Metadata - Gen 43/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mirror_tied_phase_chain                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This design preserves the successful independent RY feature transformations and           │
│                          │ open-chain CZ entanglement while imposing a stronger symmetry on the phase layers. Each   │
│                          │ post-entanglement RZ now reuses the corresponding even- or odd-parity pre-entanglement    │
│                          │ parameter. This creates a mirrored phase structure with only two RZ angles per block,     │
│                          │ substantially reducing parameter count without removing gates or connectivity. The        │
│                          │ stronger regularization is intended to retain the current validation accuracy while       │
