│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ brickwork_ring_entanglement                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the two overlapping eight-CZ layers with complementary four-CZ matchings. The     │
│                          │ first matching couples (0,1), (2,3), (4,5), and (6,7); after the noncommuting RY mixer,   │
│                          │ the shifted matching couples (1,2), (3,4), (5,6), and (7,0). Together they retain full    │
│                          │ ring connectivity while every CZ within a matching can execute in parallel. The shifted   │
│                          │ layer also couples opposite parities instead of preserving the disconnected even/odd      │
│                          │ sectors of the distance-two layer. This reduces gate count and depth without changing the │
│                          │ parameter count, and should improve optimization speed and generalization.                │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
