│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_crz_chain                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz returns to the compact linear-chain architecture that previously achieved     │
│                          │ stronger generalization and faster convergence than the current ring-and-bridge circuit.  │
│                          │ Each CZ is followed by a CRZ whose angle is shared by edge parity: one parameter for      │
│                          │ (0–1, 2–3, 4–5, 6–7) and one for (1–2, 3–4, 5–6). This adds only two trainable parameters │
│                          │ per block while allowing the optimizer to continuously tune pairwise phase correlations.  │
│                          │ The initial independent RY rotations preserve local expressivity, parity-shared           │
│                          │ pre-phases regularize the representation, and independent post-phases retain              │
│                          │ wire-specific refinement.                                                                 │
