│ patch_description        │ This design keeps the effective ingredients of the stronger current circuit—local feature │
│                          │ adaptation, parity-aware regularization, full-chain connectivity, and a noncommuting      │
│                          │ output mixer—while removing its three redundant phase-entangling sandwiches. A single     │
│                          │ linear CZ backbone is augmented immediately on every edge by commuting CRZ correlations,  │
│                          │ using only two shared parameters for alternating even and odd bonds. Independent RY       │
│                          │ angles retain local expressivity, while shared pre-entanglement RZ and post-entanglement  │
│                          │ RX rotations constrain parameter growth and should reduce overfitting. The resulting      │
│                          │ block is substantially smaller than the current ansatz, targeting better parameter        │
│                          │ efficiency, lower depth and gate count, and faster convergence without sacrificing        │
│                          │ full-chain correlation coverage.                                                          │
