│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ backward_nearest_neighbor_bridge                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the parity-preserving distance-two CZ ring with a backward nearest-neighbor       │
│                          │ chain. The current bridge separates even and odd qubits into disconnected entanglement    │
│                          │ subgraphs, which can limit cross-parity feature mixing and may contribute to slow         │
│                          │ convergence. Re-entangling adjacent qubits after the noncommuting RY mixer enables local  │
│                          │ correlations to be refined across both parity classes, while removing the ring-closure    │
│                          │ gate slightly reduces depth and gate count. The backward ordering also tests the          │
│                          │ complementary correlation layout suggested by the stronger chain-based prior architecture │
│                          │ without adding parameters.                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0603                                                                                   │
