│ patch_description        │ Insert a parity-shared RY mixer followed by a shifted, disjoint CZ matching before the    │
│                          │ final phase layer. The RY layer does not commute with the preceding phase-based CRZ       │
│                          │ structure, allowing learned phase correlations to influence populations before another    │
│                          │ entangling stage. Sharing one angle across even wires and one across odd wires adds only  │
│                          │ two parameters per block, while the shifted bonds connect correlations across the         │
│                          │ boundaries of the original chain pattern and restore ring closure. Using four disjoint CZ │
│                          │ gates limits the added depth relative to a full sequential chain.                         │
