│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ globally_tied_phase_echo                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This design retains the strongest prior program’s multi-scale CZ connectivity while       │
│                          │ applying substantially stronger parameter regularization. Instead of assigning            │
│                          │ independent phase parameters to each entangling stage, every stage reuses one             │
│                          │ parity-shared pre-phase pair and one parity-shared post-phase pair. This directly tests   │
│                          │ whether the useful behavior comes from the repeated phase-entanglement pattern rather     │
│                          │ than stage-specific angles.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The circuit combines even-bond, shifted-bond, and full-chain entanglers so information    │
│                          │ can propagate across the ring, but uses only 14 independent parameters per ansatz block:  │
│                          │ eight local RY angles, four globally shared phase angles, and two parity-shared final RX  │
│                          │ angles. The final noncommuting RX layer converts accumulated phase correlations into      │
│                          │ measurable population differences. Compared with the best prior phase-sandwich circuit,   │
│                          │ this preserves its connectivity and depth profile while sharply reducing parameter count, │
│                          │ which should improve parameter efficiency and constrain overfitting.                      │
