├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ butterfly_multiscale_mixer                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz replaces the repeated nearest-neighbor phase sandwiches with a multiscale     │
│                          │ butterfly network. Three parallel interaction stages couple distances 1, 2, and 4,        │
│                          │ allowing information to propagate globally across all eight qubits with logarithmic       │
│                          │ interaction depth. Shared CRY parameters provide trainable, non-diagonal correlations at  │
│                          │ each spatial scale while limiting model capacity. A reversed CNOT butterfly redistributes │
│                          │ the learned global parities, and a final RX→RY two-axis mixer converts phase and          │
│                          │ correlation information into measurable populations. The design uses fewer trainable      │
│                          │ parameters than the current circuit and should improve parameter efficiency and           │
│                          │ generalization while retaining expressive global interactions.                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
