│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parity_mixer_shifted_ring                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add a parameter-efficient parity-shared RY mixer after the existing phase-entangling      │
│                          │ block, followed by a shifted CZ matching that closes the qubit ring and a final           │
│                          │ parity-shared RX mixer. The mid-circuit RY layer converts learned phase information into  │
│                          │ populations before additional entanglement, while the shifted matching propagates         │
│                          │ correlations across bonds missing from the original linear CZ chain. The orthogonal final │
│                          │ RX layer further increases noncommuting expressivity. Parameter sharing limits the        │
│                          │ addition to four trainable parameters per repeated block, aiming to improve validation    │
│                          │ accuracy and convergence without excessive overfitting.                                   │
