│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_axis_final_mixer                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Append a parameter-efficient, parity-shared RX→RY output mixer after the final phase      │
│                          │ layer. The current circuit ends with RZ rotations, which may leave learned phase          │
│                          │ information poorly exposed to a population-based readout. Two noncommuting rotation axes  │
│                          │ convert those phases into measurable populations more flexibly than a single-axis mixer,  │
│                          │ while parity sharing adds only four trainable parameters per repeated block. This targets │
│                          │ the current validation gap and slow convergence without substantially increasing          │
│                          │ capacity.                                                                                 │
