│ patch_name               │ parity_rx_premixer                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Prepend a parity-shared RX layer before the existing independent RY rotations. Because RX │
│                          │ and RY do not commute, this introduces an early two-axis mixer that can create richer     │
│                          │ local states before phase rotations and CZ entanglement. Sharing one angle across even    │
│                          │ wires and one across odd wires adds only two parameters per repeated block, providing     │
│                          │ structured regularization while potentially reducing the current train-validation gap and │
│                          │ accelerating convergence.                                                                 │
